# .dockerignore (project root)
#
# NOTE: docker-compose builds each service from its own context
# (./client and ./server - see docker-compose.yml), and Docker only
# honors a .dockerignore file that lives IN that build context. That
# means client/.dockerignore and server/.dockerignore are the ones that
# actually apply day to day; this root-level file exists for parity
# with the requested project structure and covers you if you ever build
# an image directly from the repo root (e.g. `docker build .` for some
# other tooling).

node_modules
**/node_modules

dist
build
**/dist

.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
**/.env
**/.env.local

logs
**/logs
*.log

uploads/patients/*
uploads/lab-reports/*
uploads/misc/*
!uploads/**/.gitkeep

.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea

README.md
docker-compose.yml
